          "why_it_matters": "The argument is in the transformation itself: Rogiński strips Coltrane down to one untreated electric guitar and rebuilds the music through space, blues feeling, folk memory and improvisation, then extends that listening frame toward Langston Hughes. Sarah Hughes adds a separate local improviser's voice rooted in reeds and a deliberately genre-free approach. In Rhizome's close room, the night is about how familiar source material changes when timbre, silence and instrumental identity carry almost all of the weight.",
